{"audio": "1corinthians-03.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 154267, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1867, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Three."}, {"start_ms": 1867, "end_ms": 8667, "text": "And I, brethren, could not speak unto you as unto spiritual, but as unto carnal, even as unto babes in Christ."}, {"start_ms": 8667, "end_ms": 15867, "text": "I have fed you with milk, and not with meat: for hitherto ye were not able to bear it, neither yet now are ye able."}, {"start_ms": 15867, "end_ms": 24533, "text": "For ye are yet carnal: for whereas there is among you envying, and strife, and divisions, are ye not carnal, and walk as men?"}, {"start_ms": 24533, "end_ms": 30533, "text": "For while one saith, I am of Paul; and another, I am of Apollos; are ye not carnal?"}, {"start_ms": 30533, "end_ms": 37733, "text": "Who then is Paul, and who is Apollos, but ministers by whom ye believed, even as the Lord gave to every man?"}, {"start_ms": 37733, "end_ms": 41733, "text": "I have planted, Apollos watered; but God gave the increase."}, {"start_ms": 41733, "end_ms": 48533, "text": "So then neither is he that planteth any thing, neither he that watereth; but God that giveth the increase."}, {"start_ms": 48533, "end_ms": 55333, "text": "Now he that planteth and he that watereth are one: and every man shall receive his own reward according to his own labour."}, {"start_ms": 55333, "end_ms": 61867, "text": "For we are labourers together with God: ye are God's husbandry, ye are God's building."}, {"start_ms": 61867, "end_ms": 69733, "text": "According to the grace of God which is given unto me, as a wise masterbuilder, I have laid the foundation, and another buildeth thereon."}, {"start_ms": 69733, "end_ms": 72800, "text": "But let every man take heed how he buildeth thereupon."}, {"start_ms": 72800, "end_ms": 77733, "text": "For other foundation can no man lay than that is laid, which is Jesus Christ."}, {"start_ms": 77733, "end_ms": 92533, "text": "Now if any man build upon this foundation gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, stubble; Every man's work shall be made manifest: for the day shall declare it, because it shall be revealed by fire; and the fire shall try every man's work of what sort it is."}, {"start_ms": 92533, "end_ms": 97467, "text": "If any man's work abide which he hath built thereupon, he shall receive a reward."}, {"start_ms": 97467, "end_ms": 104933, "text": "If any man's work shall be burned, he shall suffer loss: but he himself shall be saved; yet so as by fire."}, {"start_ms": 104933, "end_ms": 110267, "text": "Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you?"}, {"start_ms": 110267, "end_ms": 117333, "text": "If any man defile the temple of God, him shall God destroy; for the temple of God is holy, which temple ye are."}, {"start_ms": 117333, "end_ms": 119733, "text": "Let no man deceive himself."}, {"start_ms": 119733, "end_ms": 126000, "text": "If any man among you seemeth to be wise in this world, let him become a fool, that he may be wise."}, {"start_ms": 126000, "end_ms": 129200, "text": "For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God."}, {"start_ms": 129200, "end_ms": 133733, "text": "For it is written, He taketh the wise in their own craftiness."}, {"start_ms": 133733, "end_ms": 137067, "text": "And again, The Lord knoweth the thoughts of the wise, that they are vain."}, {"start_ms": 137067, "end_ms": 139733, "text": "Therefore let no man glory in men."}, {"start_ms": 139733, "end_ms": 154267, "text": "For all things are yours; Whether Paul, or Apollos, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or things present, or things to come; all are yours; And ye are Christ's; and Christ is God's."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 602, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 602, "e": 1104, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1144, "e": 1445, "si": 0}, {"t": "Three.", "s": 1486, "e": 1747, "si": 0}, {"t": "And", "s": 2288, "e": 2368, "si": 1}, {"t": "I,", "